From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:06:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: parallel entity tracker

Behind async.parallel-tracker.enabled (default false). With the key off,
ChunkMap#tick runs Paper's tracker; the only shared edit is the visibility
test of TrackedEntity#updatePlayer moved, unchanged, into btc$visibleTo.

With the key on, a pool works out read-only which entities changed audience,
the tick thread waits for every batch, then runs Paper's own moonrise$tick
and sendChanges for them, in Paper's order. Nothing is mutated or sent from
a pool thread.

Derived from DivineMC, patch "Parallel entity tracker" (NONPLAYT, BX Team),
GPL-3.0, https://github.com/BX-Team/DivineMC - itself derived from Petal's
multithreaded tracker (peaches94, GPL-3.0), https://github.com/Bloom-host/Petal.
DivineMC's off-thread sendChanges phase is not ported.

